---
import DocsNav from "../components/DocsNav.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { evidenceHighlights, evidenceLevels, repositoryUrl } from "../data/site";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Evidence | Loom Infer"
  description="Bounded correctness and performance records for Loom Infer providers."
  active="Evidence"
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Evidence</p>
    <h1>Every number keeps its boundary.</h1>
    <p>
      A result fixes source, hardware, contract, baseline, measurement, raw
      samples, and excluded claims.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="docs-layout">
    <DocsNav active="Evidence" />
    <article class="prose">
      <h2>Evidence levels</h2>
      <div class="evidence-level-grid">
        {evidenceLevels.map((item) => (
          <div class="evidence-level-card">
            <span>{item.level}</span>
            <div><h3>{item.name}</h3><p>{item.detail}</p></div>
            <small>{item.status}</small>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <h2>Current evidence status</h2>
      <table class="evidence-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Result</th><th>Direction</th><th>Contract</th><th>Boundary</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {evidenceHighlights.map((item) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{item.value}</td>
              <td>{item.label}</td>
              <td>{item.detail}</td>
              <td>{item.sample}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <div class="doc-note">
        <strong>Loom device correctness and provider performance are separate.</strong>
        <p>
          Existing device records retain their claims for their recorded source
          trees. They do not qualify the current DeviceRegion submission path.
          Attention rankings need a new common-oracle run. Fused append still
          needs one provider-neutral oracle before it can publish a ranking.
        </p>
        <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/results/h20-bf16-paged-prefill-correctness-20260807.json`}>Correctness record</a>
        <span> · </span>
        <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/results/h20-flashinfer-v0.6.16.post1-paged-prefill-graph-performance-20260807.json`}>Graph performance record</a>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-note warning">
        <strong>Older matched attention results are historical.</strong>
        <p>
          The comparison tools poison Graph outputs, check both providers
          against one F32 reference, and reject mixed run contracts. Fused
          append also needs new sanitizer evidence for exclusive pages.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Current exclusions</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No result proves model or serving speedup.</li>
        <li>Eager provider timing is not isolated kernel timing.</li>
        <li>Graph results cover fixed addresses and named paths only.</li>
        <li>H20 results do not qualify other GPU architectures.</li>
        <li>One shape does not establish a universal provider winner.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Read the complete <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/results/README.md`}>evidence index</a>
        for source hashes, fixtures, raw samples, and exclusions.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
